  "answer_text": "It looks like you may be referring to **Iuka, Mississippi** (sometimes misspelled as \"Luka\"). Here's an overview:\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udfd9\ufe0f Iuka, Mississippi\n\n- **Iuka** (/a\u026a\u02c8ju\u02d0k\u0259/) is a city and the county seat of **Tishomingo County, Mississippi**, United States.\n\n- Its population was **3,139** at the 2020 census.\n\n- **Woodall Mountain**, the highest point in Mississippi, is located just south of Iuka.\n\n- Iuka is built on the site of a **Chickasaw village**, and the name \"Iuka\" comes from the name of one of the chiefs of that village.\n\n- Iuka was founded by **David Hubbard**, a wagon train scout, and Euro-American settlers arrived with the **Memphis and Charleston Railroad** in 1857.\n\n- The Civil War brought widespread devastation when a major engagement occurred on **September 19, 1862** \u2014 the **Battle of Iuka** \u2014 resulting in 1,200 to 1,500 killed or wounded.\n\n- **Six artesian springs** flow to the surface in Iuka at the **Iuka Springs Park**, though currently only three springs are still flowing.\n\n---\n\nCould you clarify what you were looking for? For example:\n- The **city of Iuka, MS**?\n- A specific person named **Luka** from Mississippi?\n- Something else entirely?",
